            "explanation": "Python uses indentation to identify blocks of code. It is case-sensitive, meaning 'name' and 'Name' are different identifiers. Strings must be enclosed within quotes.",
            "hint": "Think about code blocks, uppercase vs lowercase letters, and how text values are written in Python."
