    {
      "id": "M001-python-regex",
      "title": "Regular Expressions (Regex) in Python",
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What is Regular Expression (Regex)?",
            "explanation": "In the previous lessons, you learned how to work with Python strings. Sometimes, we don't just want to display text—we want to search, extract, validate, or replace specific patterns inside the text. This is where **Regular Expressions (Regex)** become useful.\n\nA **Regular Expression**, or **Regex**, is a sequence of characters that defines a search pattern. Instead of searching for an exact word, Regex allows us to search for patterns such as email addresses, phone numbers, dates, URLs, or specific words.\n\nPython provides a built-in module called **re** to work with Regular Expressions.\n\nRegex is widely used in AI applications for cleaning text, extracting information, validating user input, and preprocessing data before sending it to an AI model.\n\n**Example:**\n```python\nimport re\n\ntext = 'My email is john@gmail.com'\nmatch = re.search(r'\\S+@\\S+', text)\n\nprint(match.group())\n# Output: john@gmail.com\n```"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Why Do We Need Regex?",
            "explanation": "Searching text manually can be difficult when the format changes. Regex allows us to search for patterns instead of exact text.\n\nSome common uses include:\n\n• Finding email addresses.\n• Extracting phone numbers.\n• Validating passwords.\n• Finding URLs.\n• Cleaning unwanted characters.\n• Removing HTML tags.\n• Extracting dates.\n• Processing AI training data.\n\nRegex helps developers process large amounts of text quickly and accurately."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Common Regex Functions in Python",
            "explanation": "Now that you know how regular expressions work, let's learn the most commonly used functions provided by Python's **re** module.\n\n**1. re.search()** → Finds the **first match** anywhere in the text.\nExample:Extract the first number from the given string:\n```python\nimport re\ntext = 'My phone number is 9876543210'\nmatch = re.search(r'\\d+', text)\nprint(match.group())\n# Output: 9876543210\n```\n\n**2. re.findall()** → Returns **all matching patterns** as a list.\nExample:Print the list of marks:\n```python\nimport re\ntext = 'Marks: 85, 92, 78'\nprint(re.findall(r'\\d+', text))\n# Output: ['85', '92', '78']\n```\n\n**3. re.match()** → Checks if the pattern matches **only at the beginning** of the string.\nExample:Check the match object:\n```python\nimport re\ntext = 'Python is easy'\nprint(re.match(r'Python', text))\n# Output: Match object\n```\n\n**4. re.sub()** → Replaces matching text with new text.\nExample:Replace the given name:\n```python\nimport re\ntext = 'Hello John'\nprint(re.sub(r'John', 'Alice', text))\n# Output: Hello Alice\n```\n\n**5. re.split()** → Splits text based on a pattern.\nExample:split the given text:\n```python\nimport re\ntext = 'Apple,Banana,Mango'\nprint(re.split(r',', text))\n# Output: ['Apple', 'Banana', 'Mango']\n```\n\nThese five functions cover most real-world regex tasks such as searching text, extracting information, replacing text, and splitting strings."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Meta Characters in RegEx",
            "explanation": "",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;\"><h2 style=\"text-align:center;color:#60a5fa;margin-bottom:10px;\">Common Regex Characters</h2><p style=\"text-align:center;color:#cbd5e1;margin-bottom:20px;\">Each example shows the input text, the regex pattern, and the matching output.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background:#2563eb;\"><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Regex</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Meaning</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Example</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>[ ]</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches any character inside the brackets.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'cat bat mat'</code><br>Regex = <code>[cb]at</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['cat','bat']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>\\d</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches any digit (0-9).</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'Order 123'</code><br>Regex = <code>\\d+</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['123']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>.</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches any single character.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'hat hot hit'</code><br>Regex = <code>h.t</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['hat','hot','hit']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>^</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches the beginning of a string.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'hello world'</code><br>Regex = <code>^hello</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['hello']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>$</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches the end of a string.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'welcome home'</code><br>Regex = <code>home$</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['home']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>*</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches zero or more occurrences.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'heo heeeo ho'</code><br>Regex = <code>he*o</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['heo','heeeo','ho']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>+</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches one or more occurrences.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'heo heeeo ho'</code><br>Regex = <code>he+o</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['heo','heeeo']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>?</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches zero or one occurrence.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'color colour'</code><br>Regex = <code>colou?r</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['color','colour']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>{}</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches an exact number of occurrences.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'heo heeo heeeo'</code><br>Regex = <code>he{2}o</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['heeo']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>|</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches either pattern.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'cat dog bird'</code><br>Regex = <code>cat|dog</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['cat','dog']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>()</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Groups patterns together.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Sentence = <code>'Mr John'</code><br>Regex = <code>(Mr) (John)</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">Group1='Mr', Group2='John'</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"margin-top:20px;background:#1e293b;padding:15px;border-left:5px solid #22c55e;border-radius:8px;\"><b>💡 Tip:</b> Regex does not search for exact words. It searches for <b>patterns</b>. That's why it is widely used in AI, NLP, document processing, and data extraction.</div></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Regex Special Sequences",
            "explanation": "Now that you know what Regular Expressions are, let's learn about **Special Sequences**.\n\nSpecial sequences are **shortcuts** that help us match common types of characters without writing long patterns.\n\nHere are the most commonly used special sequences:\n\n**\\d** → Matches any digit (0-9).\nExample: `\\d+` matches `25` or `2025`.\n\n**\\D** → Matches any character that is **not** a digit.\nExample: `\\D+` matches `Python`.\n\n**\\w** → Matches letters, numbers, and underscores.\nExample: `\\w+` matches `user_123`.\n\n**\\W** → Matches any character that is **not** a letter, number, or underscore.\nExample: `\\W` matches `@` or `#`.\n\n**\\s** → Matches whitespace such as spaces, tabs, or new lines.\nExample: `\\s` matches the space in `Hello World`.\n\n**\\S** → Matches any character that is **not** a whitespace.\nExample: `\\S+` matches `Hello`.\n\nThese shortcuts make regex patterns much shorter and easier to read.\n\n**Example:**\n```python\nimport re\n\ntext = 'User123 has 250 points'\n\nprint(re.findall(r'\\d+', text))   # ['123', '250']\nprint(re.findall(r'\\w+', text))   # ['User123', 'has', '250', 'points']\nprint(re.findall(r'\\s', text))    # [' ', ' ', ' ']\n```"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Common Regex Patterns",
            "explanation": "Regex uses special symbols called **metacharacters**. These symbols help us search, match, and extract text patterns efficiently. The table below explains the most commonly used Regex patterns with simple examples.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;\"><h2 style=\"text-align:center;color:#60a5fa;margin-bottom:10px;\">Common Regex Patterns</h2><p style=\"text-align:center;color:#cbd5e1;margin-bottom:20px;\">Understand the most frequently used Regex metacharacters with simple examples.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;\"><thead><tr style=\"background:#2563eb;\"><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Pattern</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Meaning</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Example</th><th style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>.</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches any single character.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'cat bat hat'</code><br>Regex = <code>.at</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['cat','bat','hat']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>\\d</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches any digit (0-9).</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'Age 25'</code><br>Regex = <code>\\d+</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['25']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>\\w</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches letters, numbers, and underscore.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'user_123'</code><br>Regex = <code>\\w+</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['user_123']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>\\s</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches whitespace.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'Hello World'</code><br>Regex = <code>\\s</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">[' ']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>+</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">One or more occurrences.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'heeello'</code><br>Regex = <code>e+</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['eeee']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>*</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Zero or more occurrences.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'ho hello'</code><br>Regex = <code>he*o</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['ho']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>?</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Zero or one occurrence.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'color colour'</code><br>Regex = <code>colou?r</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['color','colour']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>^</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches the beginning of a string.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'Python Regex'</code><br>Regex = <code>^Python</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['Python']</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><b>$</b></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Matches the end of a string.</td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;\">Text = <code>'Learn Regex'</code><br>Regex = <code>Regex$</code></td><td style=\"padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;\">['Regex']</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"margin-top:20px;background:#1e293b;padding:15px;border-left:5px solid #22c55e;border-radius:8px;\"><b>💡 Remember:</b> Regex patterns are combined to create powerful search expressions. For example, <code>^\\d+$</code> matches a string that contains only digits, while <code>\\w+@\\w+\\.com</code> can match simple email addresses.</div></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Regex Basics",
            "question": "Complete the statements.",
            "template": [
              "Python uses the ______ module for Regular Expressions.",
              "______ returns all matching patterns.",
              "\\d represents any ______."
            ],
            "options": [
              "re",
              "findall",
              "digit",
              "string"
            ],
            "answers": {
              "blank1": "re",
              "blank2": "findall",
              "blank3": "digit"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Using Regex for Data Preprocessing",
            "explanation": "Now that you know how to search patterns using Regex, let's see one of its most important real-world uses: **Data Preprocessing**.\n\nBefore sending text to an AI model, the data is often messy. It may contain email addresses, phone numbers, URLs, special characters, or extra spaces. If we send this noisy data directly to an AI model, the results may not be accurate.\n\nThis is where Regex becomes useful. It helps us clean the text before processing it.\n\nLet's understand the steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Start with the raw text.\n\n**Step 2:** Remove unwanted patterns such as email addresses, phone numbers, or URLs.\n\n**Step 3:** Remove extra spaces and special characters.\n\n**Step 4:** The cleaned text is now ready for AI models, text analysis, or machine learning.\n\n**Example:**\n```python\nimport re\n\ntext = \"Contact me at john@gmail.com or visit https://example.com Call: 9876543210\"\n\n# Step 1: Remove email addresses\ntext = re.sub(r'\\S+@\\S+', '', text)\n\n# Step 2: Remove URLs\ntext = re.sub(r'https?://\\S+', '', text)\n\n# Step 3: Remove phone numbers\ntext = re.sub(r'\\d{10}', '', text)\n\n# Step 4: Remove extra spaces\ntext = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n\nprint(text)\n# Output:\n# Contact me at or visit Call:\n```\n\nIn real-world AI applications such as chatbots, document processing, sentiment analysis, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Regex is often the first step used to clean text before generating embeddings or sending it to an LLM."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Test your understanding of Python Regex by completing this coding challenge.\n\nInstructions:\n1. Import the `re` module.\n2. Create a variable `txt` with the value \"Welcome to Python Regex\".\n3. Search for the word `Python` in `txt` and store the result in a variable named `x`.\n4. Print the position (span) of the matched word.",
            "starterCode": "# Import the required module\n\n# Create a string\n\n# Search for the word 'Python'\n\n# Print the position of the matched word\n",
            "solution": "# Import the regular expression module\nimport re\n\n# Create a string to search in\ntxt = \"Welcome to Python Regex\"\n\n# Search for the word 'Python'\nx = re.search(r\"Python\", txt)\n\n# Print the starting and ending position of the match\nprint(x.span())",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Use `re.search()` to find the word and `span()` to display its start and end positions."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Test your understanding of Regex for data preprocessing.\n\nInstructions:\n1. Import the `re` module.\n2. Create a variable `text` with the value \"Contact us at support@company.com or call 9876543210\".\n3. Remove the email address using `re.sub()`.\n4. Remove the phone number using `re.sub()`.\n5. Print the cleaned text.",
            "starterCode": "import re\n\n# Create the input text\ntext = \"\"\n\n# Remove the email address\n\n# Remove the phone number\n\n# Print the cleaned text\nprint(text)",
            "solution": "# Import the regular expression module\nimport re\n\n# Create the input text\ntext = \"Contact us at support@company.com or call 9876543210\"\n\n# Remove the email address\ntext = re.sub(r\"\\S+@\\S+\", \"\", text)\n\n# Remove the phone number\ntext = re.sub(r\"\\d{10}\", \"\", text)\n\n# Print the cleaned text\nprint(text)",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Use `re.sub()` to replace both the email address and the 10-digit phone number with an empty string."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "Which Python module is used for Regex?",
