    {
      "id": "M003-dl-lesson-7-cnn-architectures",
      "title": "CNN Architectures & Evolution",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#ea580c",
        "accent": "#c2410c"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What is CNN Architecture?",
            "explanation": "Now that we have learned individual CNN components like Convolution, Pooling, and Flatten, let's see how they work together as a complete CNN architecture.\n**CNN Architecture** is the overall structure of a Convolutional Neural Network. It is made up of different layers that work together to analyze images and identify objects.\n\nA CNN learns in stages:\n• Early layers detect simple patterns like edges and corners.\n• Middle layers detect shapes and textures.\n• Deeper layers recognize complex objects and important features.\n• Final layers use these learned features to make predictions.\n\nKey Idea: CNN architecture organizes different layers so the network can gradually learn from simple patterns to complex objects."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "CNN Architecture: The End-to-End Flow",
            "explanation": "`How CNN Architeture works:`\n• Input Image . The process starts with a raw image (example: a bird or object image).\n• Kernel (Filter) . A small matrix slides over the image to detect patterns.\n• Convolution Layer . Extracts basic features like edges, curves, and textures from the image.\n• Feature Maps . The output of convolution showing detected patterns in different regions.\n• Pooling Layer . Reduces the size of feature maps while keeping important information (downsampling).\n• Convolution + Pooling Repeat . The network goes deeper and learns more complex patterns like shapes and object parts.\n• Deep Feature Maps . Higher-level representations of the image are formed.\n• Flatten Layer . Converts all 2D feature maps into a single 1D vector.\n• Fully Connected Layer (Dense Layer) . Combines all extracted features to understand what the image represents.\n• Classification Layer . Processes learned features to prepare final decision scores.\n• Softmax Output . Converts scores into probabilities for each class (example: Donald, Goofy, Tweety).\n• Final Prediction . The class with the highest probability is selected as output.\n\nKey Idea . CNN works by first extracting simple features in early layers and then learning complex object representations in deeper layers.",
            "html_code": "<div style='background:#fdfaf0; border:1px solid #e2e8f0; width:100%; overflow-x:auto; font-family:sans-serif; box-shadow:0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);'><svg viewBox='0 0 900 450' style='width:100%; min-width:800px; height:auto;'><defs><marker id='arrow-blue' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='5' refY='5' markerWidth='6' markerHeight='6' orient='auto-start-reverse'><path d='M 0 2 L 10 5 L 0 8 z' fill='#3b82f6'/></marker></defs><text x='450' y='35' font-size='18' font-weight='bold' font-style='italic' text-decoration='underline' fill='#1e3a8a' text-anchor='middle'>A Typical Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)</text><text x='145' y='100' font-size='12' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Convolution</text><text x='245' y='100' font-size='12' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Pooling</text><text x='350' y='100' font-size='12' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Convolution</text><text x='460' y='100' font-size='12' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Pooling</text><rect x='20' y='130' width='75' height='75' fill='#fef08a' stroke='#eab308' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='57' y='180' font-size='45' text-anchor='middle'>🐥</text><text x='57' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Input Image</text><g stroke='#1e40af' fill='#60a5fa' stroke-width='1'><rect x='150' y='125' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='140' y='132' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='130' y='140' width='40' height='65'/></g><text x='145' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Featured</text><text x='145' y='285' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>maps</text><g stroke='#166534' fill='#4ade80' stroke-width='1'><rect x='250' y='135' width='35' height='55'/><rect x='240' y='142' width='35' height='55'/><rect x='230' y='150' width='35' height='55'/></g><text x='245' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Pooled</text><text x='245' y='285' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Featured maps</text><g stroke='#a16207' fill='#facc15' stroke-width='1'><rect x='370' y='120' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='360' y='127' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='350' y='134' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='340' y='141' width='40' height='65'/><rect x='330' y='148' width='40' height='65'/></g><text x='350' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Featured</text><text x='350' y='285' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>maps</text><g stroke='#c2410c' fill='#f97316' stroke-width='1'><rect x='480' y='130' width='30' height='50'/><rect x='470' y='137' width='30' height='50'/><rect x='460' y='144' width='30' height='50'/><rect x='450' y='151' width='30' height='50'/><rect x='440' y='158' width='30' height='50'/></g><text x='460' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Pooled</text><text x='460' y='285' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Featured maps</text><text x='585' y='270' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Flatten</text><text x='585' y='285' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>layer</text><g fill='#94a3b8' stroke='#475569'><rect x='577' y='100' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='120' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='140' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='160' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='180' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='200' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='220' width='16' height='16'/><rect x='577' y='240' width='16' height='16'/></g><g stroke='#60a5fa' stroke-width='1.2' opacity='0.8'><path d='M 593 108 L 660 80 M 593 108 L 660 140 M 593 108 L 660 230' /><path d='M 593 148 L 660 80 M 593 148 L 660 170 M 593 148 L 660 260 M 593 148 L 660 110 M 593 148 L 660 200 M 593 148 L 660 290'/><path d='M 593 188 L 660 110 M 593 188 L 660 200 M 593 188 L 660 290'/><path d='M 593 248 L 660 140 M 593 248 L 660 230 M 593 248 L 660 290'/><path d='M 680 80 L 730 135 M 680 80 L 730 185 M 680 80 L 730 235'/><path d='M 680 140 L 730 135 M 680 140 L 730 185 M 680 140 L 730 235'/><path d='M 680 200 L 730 135 M 680 200 L 730 185 M 680 200 L 730 235'/><path d='M 680 260 L 730 135 M 680 260 L 730 185 M 680 260 L 730 235'/></g><g stroke='#60a5fa' stroke-width='1.5'><line x1='750' y1='135' x2='800' y2='135' /><line x1='750' y1='185' x2='800' y2='185' /><line x1='750' y1='235' x2='800' y2='235' /></g><g fill='#60a5fa' stroke='#1e40af' stroke-width='1'><circle cx='670' cy='80' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='110' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='140' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='170' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='200' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='230' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='260' r='10'/><circle cx='670' cy='290' r='10'/></g><g fill='#60a5fa' stroke='#1e40af' stroke-width='1'><circle cx='740' cy='135' r='10'/><circle cx='740' cy='185' r='10'/><circle cx='740' cy='235' r='10'/></g><text x='775' y='139' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>0.2</text><text x='775' y='189' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>0.1</text><text x='775' y='239' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>0.7</text><text x='835' y='90' font-size='14' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Output</text><g fill='#60a5fa' stroke='#1e40af' stroke-width='1'><rect x='800' y='115' width='70' height='40' rx='8'/><rect x='800' y='165' width='70' height='40' rx='8'/><rect x='800' y='215' width='70' height='40' rx='8'/></g><text x='835' y='139' font-size='12' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>Donald</text><text x='835' y='189' font-size='12' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>Goofy</text><text x='835' y='239' font-size='12' fill='#0f172a' text-anchor='middle'>Tweety</text><rect x='75' y='185' width='15' height='15' fill='none' stroke='#ef4444' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='82.5' y='240' font-size='11' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Kernel</text><line x1='82.5' y1='205' x2='82.5' y2='225' stroke='#94a3b8' stroke-width='1.5'/><rect x='155' y='155' width='12' height='12' fill='none' stroke='#ef4444' stroke-width='1.5'/><path d='M 90 185 L 155 155 M 90 200 L 155 167' stroke='#0f172a' stroke-dasharray='6 4' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='250' y='195' width='12' height='12' fill='none' stroke='#ef4444' stroke-width='1.5'/><rect x='360' y='170' width='12' height='12' fill='none' stroke='#ef4444' stroke-width='1.5'/><path d='M 262 195 L 360 170 M 262 207 L 360 182' stroke='#0f172a' stroke-dasharray='6 4' stroke-width='2'/><path d='M 470 158 L 577 100 M 470 208 L 577 256' stroke='#0f172a' stroke-dasharray='6 4' stroke-width='2'/><line x1='130' y1='330' x2='550' y2='330' stroke='#3b82f6' stroke-width='2' marker-start='url(#arrow-blue)' marker-end='url(#arrow-blue)'/><text x='340' y='345' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Feature Maps</text><line x1='640' y1='330' x2='770' y2='330' stroke='#3b82f6' stroke-width='2' marker-start='url(#arrow-blue)' marker-end='url(#arrow-blue)'/><text x='705' y='345' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Fully connected layer</text><path d='M 40 380 L 40 390 L 580 390 L 580 380' fill='none' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='310' y='415' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Feature Extraction</text><path d='M 610 380 L 610 390 L 740 390 L 740 380' fill='none' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='675' y='415' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Classification</text><path d='M 760 380 L 760 390 L 890 390 L 890 380' fill='none' stroke='#64748b' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='825' y='410' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>Probabilistic</text><text x='825' y='425' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='#0f172a'>distribution</text></svg></div>",
            "example": "# CNN Architecture\nmodel = Sequential([\n    Conv2D(32, (3,3), activation='relu', input_shape=(224,224,3)),\n    MaxPooling2D((2,2)),\n    Flatten(),\n    Dense(128, activation='relu'),\n    Dense(10, activation='softmax')\n])\n\n`Workflow:`\nInput Image → Conv2D → ReLU → MaxPooling → Flatten → Dense → Softmax\n\n`Use Case:` Image Classification, Face Recognition, Medical Imaging"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Implementation of CNN (MNIST Digit Classifier)",
            "explanation": "Now that you understand how Convolutional Neural Networks work,Let's build our first Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to classify handwritten digits using the **MNIST** dataset.\n\nBefore writing any code, create a new project folder and create a file named **main.py**.\n\n### Step 1: Install Required Libraries\nOpen the terminal and install TensorFlow:\n`pip install tensorflow`\n\n### Step 2: Import Required Libraries\n\n```python\nimport tensorflow as tf\nfrom tensorflow.keras import layers, models\nfrom tensorflow.keras.datasets import mnist\n```\n\nThese libraries allow us to load the MNIST dataset and build a CNN model.\n\n### Step 3: Load the Dataset\n\n```python\n(train_images, train_labels), (test_images, test_labels) = mnist.load_data()\n```\n\nThe MNIST dataset is automatically downloaded the first time you run this code.\n\nIt contains:\n\n• 60,000 training images\n• 10,000 testing images\n• Each image is 28 × 28 pixels\n• There are 10 classes (digits 0–9)\n\nLet's verify the dataset.\n\n```python\nprint(train_images.shape)\nprint(train_labels.shape)\n\nprint(test_images.shape)\nprint(test_labels.shape)\n```\n\nExpected Output:\n\n```\n(60000, 28, 28)\n(60000,)\n(10000, 28, 28)\n(10000,)\n```\n\n### Step 4: Preprocess the Images\n\n```python\ntrain_images = train_images.reshape((60000, 28, 28, 1)).astype('float32') / 255\n\ntest_images = test_images.reshape((10000, 28, 28, 1)).astype('float32') / 255\n```\n\nWe reshape the images to include the color channel and normalize pixel values from **0–255** to **0–1**, which helps the CNN learn faster.\n\n### Step 5: Build the CNN Model\n\n```python\nmodel = models.Sequential([\n    layers.Conv2D(32, (3,3), activation='relu', input_shape=(28,28,1)),\n    layers.MaxPooling2D((2,2)),\n\n    layers.Conv2D(64, (3,3), activation='relu'),\n    layers.MaxPooling2D((2,2)),\n\n    layers.Conv2D(64, (3,3), activation='relu'),\n\n    layers.Flatten(),\n\n    layers.Dense(64, activation='relu'),\n\n    layers.Dense(10, activation='softmax')\n])\n```\n\n### Step 6: Compile the Model\n\n```python\nmodel.compile(\n    optimizer='adam',\n    loss='sparse_categorical_crossentropy',\n    metrics=['accuracy']\n)\n```\n\nNow our CNN architecture is ready. In the next lesson, we'll train the model, evaluate its performance, and use it to predict handwritten digits."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Training, Evaluating & Predicting with CNN",
            "explanation": "Now that our CNN architecture is ready, let's train it using the MNIST training dataset.\n\n### Step 1: Train the Model\n\n```python\nhistory = model.fit(\n    train_images,\n    train_labels,\n    epochs=5,\n    batch_size=64,\n    validation_split=0.2\n)\n```\n\nDuring training:\n\n• The model learns from 80% of the training images.\n• The remaining 20% is used for validation.\n• Training continues for 5 epochs.\n\n### Step 2: Evaluate the Model\n\n```python\ntest_loss, test_acc = model.evaluate(\n    test_images,\n    test_labels\n)\n\nprint('Test Accuracy:', test_acc)\n```\n\nYou should obtain an accuracy close to **99%**, showing that the CNN has learned to recognize handwritten digits very effectively.\n\n### Step 3: Compare Training & Validation Accuracy\n\n```python\nprint(history.history['accuracy'])\nprint(history.history['val_accuracy'])\n```\n\nIf both values are high and close to each other, the model is generalizing well.\n\n### Step 4: Predict a New Digit\n\n```python\nprediction = model.predict(test_images[0:1])\n\npredicted_digit = tf.argmax(prediction[0]).numpy()\n\nprint('Predicted Digit:', predicted_digit)\nprint('Actual Digit:', test_labels[0])\n```\n\nThe model predicts the probabilities for all ten digits. We use **argmax()** to select the digit with the highest probability.\n\n### Step 5: View the Prediction\n\n```python\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nplt.imshow(test_images[0].reshape(28,28), cmap='gray')\nplt.title(f'Predicted: {predicted_digit}')\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.show()\n```\n\nThis displays the handwritten digit along with the model's prediction.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"text-align:center;padding:20px;\"><img src=\"/images/predicted_output7.png\" alt=\"predicted_output7\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #ddd;box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);\"/><p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:#555;\"><b>Figure:</b> Predicted Digit Output.</p></div>"
          }
        },
