          "type": "case_study",
          "title": "Case Study: The Resume Rejection Engine",
          "context": "A recruitment company built an ATS (Applicant Tracking System) in 2012 using a basic Count Vectorizer. The job posting specifically required a 'Software Engineer'. An expert applicant applied, but their resume stated they were a 'Backend Developer'. The ATS scored their resume match as 0% and automatically rejected them.",
          "questions": [
