        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Calculate the Cosine Similarity between two text vectors using `scikit-learn`.",
            "starterCode": "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Document Vectors (e.g., extracted from a Word2Vec model)\ndoc_A = np.array([[1.5, 0.2, 0.8]])\ndoc_B = np.array([[1.4, 0.1, 0.9]])\ndoc_C = np.array([[-0.5, 2.1, -1.2]]) # Unrelated document\n\n# TODO: Calculate the similarity between doc_A and doc_B\nsim_AB = ____(____, ____)\n\n# TODO: Calculate the similarity between doc_A and doc_C\nsim_AC = ____(____, ____)\n\nprint(f\"Similarity A to B: {sim_AB[0][0]:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"Similarity A to C: {sim_AC[0][0]:.3f}\")",
            "solution": "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Document Vectors (e.g., extracted from a Word2Vec model)\ndoc_A = np.array([[1.5, 0.2, 0.8]])\ndoc_B = np.array([[1.4, 0.1, 0.9]])\ndoc_C = np.array([[-0.5, 2.1, -1.2]]) # Unrelated document\n\n# TODO: Calculate the similarity between doc_A and doc_B\nsim_AB = cosine_similarity(doc_A, doc_B)\n\n# TODO: Calculate the similarity between doc_A and doc_C\nsim_AC = cosine_similarity(doc_A, doc_C)\n\nprint(f\"Similarity A to B: {sim_AB[0][0]:.3f}\")\nprint(f\"Similarity A to C: {sim_AC[0][0]:.3f}\")",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Pass the two numpy arrays directly into the `cosine_similarity(array1, array2)` function."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Introduction to Topic Modeling",
            "explanation": "So far, we have learned how to measure similarity between documents. Now let's learn how to automatically discover hidden themes in large collections of text.\nImagine a company has 100,000 customer support tickets. You can't read them all. You want an algorithm to automatically read them and group them into 'Topics' (e.g., Topic 1: Password Resets, Topic 2: Billing Errors, Topic 3: UI Bugs).\n\nTopic Modeling is an **Unsupervised Learning** technique. You do not give the algorithm labels. It finds the hidden, latent themes purely by analyzing which words frequently co-occur across the corpus."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "LSA (Latent Semantic Analysis)",
            "explanation": "Great! Now let's learn one of the earliest Topic Modeling techniques called **LSA (Latent Semantic Analysis)**.\nImagine you have thousands of documents containing millions of words.\nMany words may have similar meanings.\nFor example:Car,Automobile\nAlthough these are different words, they often appear in similar contexts.\n\nLSA uses a mathematical technique called **SVD (Singular Value Decomposition)** to compress large text data into a smaller representation.\nDuring this process, unnecessary noise is removed and similar words become grouped together.\n\n**Key Idea:** LSA reduces large text datasets into smaller meaningful representations using SVD."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "LDA (Latent Dirichlet Allocation)",
            "explanation": "Let's discuss,the most popular Topic Modeling algorithm is **LDA (Latent Dirichlet Allocation)**. It takes a probabilistic approach based on two brilliant assumptions:\n\n1. **Every Document is a mixture of Topics.** (e.g., A news article might be 70% Politics, 30% Economics).\n2. **Every Topic is a mixture of Words.** (e.g., The 'Politics' topic has a high probability of generating the words 'election', 'senate', 'vote').\n\nLDA reverse-engineers the corpus. It assigns words to topics and topics to documents until it finds the optimal probabilistic balance. You literally tell LDA: *\"Find me 5 topics in this dataset,\"* and it will output lists of words that describe those 5 hidden themes!",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"font-family:sans-serif; text-align:center; max-width:650px; margin:auto; padding:20px; background:#f0fdfa; border-radius:12px; border:1px solid #5eead4;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0f766e; margin-bottom:15px;\">How LDA Views a Document</h3><div style=\"background:white; padding:15px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; text-align:left; margin-bottom:20px; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;\">The <span style=\"background:#fee2e2; color:#b91c1c; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">bank</span> announced a new <span style=\"background:#fee2e2; color:#b91c1c; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">interest rate</span> policy today, causing the <span style=\"background:#fee2e2; color:#b91c1c; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">stock market</span> to jump. Meanwhile, the <span style=\"background:#dbeafe; color:#1d4ed8; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">coach</span> of the national <span style=\"background:#dbeafe; color:#1d4ed8; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">team</span> resigned after the <span style=\"background:#dbeafe; color:#1d4ed8; padding:2px 4px; border-radius:4px; font-weight:bold;\">championship</span> loss.</div><div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-around;\"><div style=\"width:45%; background:#fee2e2; padding:15px; border-radius:8px; border:2px solid #f87171;\"><h4 style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0; color:#991b1b;\">Topic 1: Finance (60%)</h4><ul style=\"text-align:left; margin:0; padding-left:20px; color:#7f1d1d; font-size:14px;\"><li>bank (0.24)</li><li>stock (0.18)</li><li>interest (0.12)</li></ul></div><div style=\"width:45%; background:#dbeafe; padding:15px; border-radius:8px; border:2px solid #60a5fa;\"><h4 style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0; color:#1e40af;\">Topic 2: Sports (40%)</h4><ul style=\"text-align:left; margin:0; padding-left:20px; color:#1e3a8a; font-size:14px;\"><li>team (0.28)</li><li>coach (0.21)</li><li>championship (0.15)</li></ul></div></div><p style=\"font-size:13px; color:#0f766e; margin-top:20px;\">LDA discovers that this single document is a 60/40 blend of two completely different latent topics.</p></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Topic Modeling Master Review",
            "question": "Fill in the blanks using the correct concepts.",
            "template": [
              "Topic Modeling is an ____ learning technique.",
              "LSA uses ____ to reduce large text datasets.",
              "LDA assumes every document contains multiple ____.",
              "In LDA, each topic is represented by a group of ____."
            ],
            "options": [
              "Unsupervised",
              "SVD",
              "topics",
              "words",
              "labels",
              "images"
            ],
            "answers": {
              "blank_1": "Unsupervised",
              "blank_2": "SVD",
