              "answer": 2,
              "explanation": "Google Gemini stands out for supporting up to 2 million tokens of context window and processing video/audio natively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Hands-On: Setting Up API Access",
            "explanation": "To build applications using model APIs, you must retrieve API keys from the model providers.\n\n**Step 1: Create an OpenAI API Key**\n1. Sign up/log in at [platform.openai.com](https://platform.openai.com).\n2. Navigate to API Keys section and click **Create new secret key**.\n3. Copy and save it. It will never be displayed again.\n\n**Step 2: Create a Groq API Key**\n1. Sign up/log in at [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com).\n2. Navigate to **API Keys** and click **Create API Key**.\n3. Copy and store it securely.\n\n**Security Best Practice:** Never hardcode your API keys in your files. Instead, load them from environment variables:\n```python\n# Save in a file named .env:\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nGROQ_API_KEY=gsk-...\n```\nUse libraries like `python-dotenv` to load them automatically in Python.",
            "tip": "If your API keys are leaked on GitHub, bots will steal them instantly and run up massive bills. Always add `.env` to your `.gitignore` file!"
          }
