        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Building a Text Summarizer",
            "explanation": "Wonderful! Now let's build another real-world LLM application.A summarizer takes long text and asks the LLM to create a shorter version.Imagine you have a 20-page article, research paper, or business report.Reading everything takes time.\nInstead, we can ask the LLM to create a shorter version while keeping the important information.This process is called Text Summarization.\n\n**Workflow:**\nDocument → Prompt → LLM → Summary",
            "example": "text = 'Artificial Intelligence is transforming industries...'\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n model='gpt-4o-mini',\n messages=[{\n 'role':'user',\n 'content':f'Summarize this text:\\n{text}'\n }]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)",
            "tip": "Specify summary length in the prompt for better results."
          }
