    {
      "id": "M006-prompt-eng-04",
      "title": "Structured Output Generation",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#f59e0b",
        "accent": "#d97706"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Babel Problem: Why Standard Text Fails",
            "explanation": "Great! So far, we have learned how to get LLMs to generate high-quality answers. But now we face a new challenge.\nImagine building an automated software pipeline. You ask an AI to extract a client's age, and it replies: *'Sure! The client is 28 years old. Let me know if you need anything else!'* \n\nIf you pass that string directly into a database expecting an integer, your entire application crashes. Humans love conversational pleasantries; software systems hate them. \n\n**Structured Output Generation** is the discipline of forcing Large Language Models to abandon human conversation and output pure, deterministic data formats (like JSON, XML, or Markdown) that can be instantly consumed by front-end UIs or backend APIs without regular expression hacks.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background: #fffbeb; border: 1px solid #fcd34d; padding: 20px; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px;\"><div style=\"background: #fef2f2; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 4px solid #ef4444;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #991b1b;\">Conversational (Breaks Code)</strong><p style=\"font-size: 12px; margin-top: 8px; color: #7f1d1d; font-family: monospace;\">\"Here is the data you requested:\\n{\\n 'name': 'Alice',\\n 'role': 'Dev'\\n}\\nHope this helps!\"</p></div><div style=\"background: #ecfdf5; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border-left: 4px solid #10b981;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #065f46;\">Structured (Code Safe)</strong><p style=\"font-size: 12px; margin-top: 8px; color: #064e3b; font-family: monospace;\">{\n  \"name\": \"Alice\",\n  \"role\": \"Dev\"\n}</p></div></div><p style=\"font-size: 12px; margin-top: 15px; color: #b45309; font-weight: bold; text-align: center;\">The goal is zero conversational wrappers.</p></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "JSON Output & Schema-Based Prompting",
            "explanation": "Now we know why structured outputs are important.But simply telling an AI 'Output JSON' is often not enough.The model may still add explanations or extra text.Professional developers solve this using **Schema-Based Prompting**. \n\nA schema is a strict blueprint. You explicitly define the keys, the data types (string, integer, boolean), and the array structures directly in the system prompt. This acts as an inescapable cage for the AI's token generation. When combined with API-level parameters like OpenAI's `response_format={ \"type\": \"json_object\" }`, the model is mathematically forced to comply.",
            "tip": "Always inject a blank JSON template directly into your prompt. Don't make the AI guess what keys your database is expecting.",
            "example": "```python\n# Schema Blueprinting Example\n\nsystem_prompt = \"\"\"\nExtract the data using strictly this schema:\n{\n  \"candidate_name\": \"string\",\n  \"ats_score\": 0,\n  \"is_qualified\": true\n}\n\nRule: Return ONLY valid JSON.\n\"\"\"\n\nuser_prompt = \"Resume: John Smith has 5 years of Python experience and matches most job requirements.\"\n\nresponse = llm.invoke([\n    {\n        \"role\": \"system\",\n        \"content\": system_prompt\n    },\n    {\n        \"role\": \"user\",\n        \"content\": user_prompt\n    }\n])\n\nprint(response)\n```"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Markdown and XML: The Other Formats",
            "explanation": "JSON is the most popular structured format, but it is not always the best choice.\nDifferent applications require different output formats.\n\n• **Markdown Output:** Perfect for front-end rendering. If you are building a React or Next.js web application and want to display rich text, tables, or code snippets, instruct the model to output strict Markdown. It is highly readable for both humans and UI components.\n• **XML Output:** If you are integrating AI into legacy enterprise systems, banking software, or SOAP APIs, JSON might be rejected. Prompting the model to wrap extractions in `<tags>` ensures compatibility with older infrastructure.",
            "example": "Instruction: Wrap the final summary inside <summary> tags, and the list of action items inside <actions> tags."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Function Calling: The Ultimate Control",
            "explanation": "Amazing! Structured outputs solve formatting problems.\nBut what if the AI needs to perform an action instead of generating text?\nFor example:\nUser: 'What's the weather in Delhi?'\nThe AI doesn't know live weather data.Instead of guessing, modern LLMs can call tools.This is called Function Calling.\nInstead of asking the model for text, you provide the model with a programmatic list of functions your application has (e.g., `check_inventory(item_id, quantity)`). The LLM realizes it needs to use that tool to fulfill the user's request, so it halts text generation and natively outputs a JSON object containing the exact arguments needed to trigger your code. You execute the code, feed the result back, and the AI continues.",
            "html_code": "<iframe style=\"width:100%; min-height:260px; border:none; background:transparent;\" srcdoc=\"<style>body{margin:0;font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:transparent;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;color:#f8fafc;}.box{background:linear-gradient(145deg, #1e1b4b, #2e1065);border:1px solid #6366f1;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;width:100%;max-width:600px;box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(99,102,241,0.2);text-align:center;}.title{margin:0 0 20px 0;color:#a5b4fc;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.5px;}.flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;}.step{background:rgba(15,23,42,0.8);border:1px solid #4f46e5;border-radius:8px;padding:16px;width:30%;position:relative;transition:transform 0.3s;}.step:hover{transform:translateY(-5px);}.step h4{margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#c084fc;font-size:14px;}.step p{margin:0;font-size:12px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.4;}.arrow{color:#ec4899;font-weight:bold;font-size:24px;animation:pulse 1.5s infinite;}@keyframes pulse{0%{transform:translateX(0);opacity:0.4;}50%{transform:translateX(6px);opacity:1;}100%{transform:translateX(0);opacity:0.4;}}.llm{border-color:#ec4899;background:rgba(236,72,153,0.1);box-shadow:inset 0 0 15px rgba(236,72,153,0.1);}.llm h4{color:#f472b6;}.code{background:#020617;padding:6px;border-radius:4px;color:#4ade80;font-family:monospace;font-size:10px;display:block;margin-top:10px;border:1px solid #334155;}</style><div class='box'><div class='title'>⚡ Function Calling Execution Flow</div><div class='flow'><div class='step'><h4>🧑‍💻 1. User Prompt</h4><p>&quot;What's the weather like in Delhi?&quot;</p></div><div class='arrow'>→</div><div class='step llm'><h4>🧠 2. LLM Decision</h4><p>Suspends generation &amp; requests a tool:</p><span class='code'>get_weather({&quot;loc&quot;: &quot;Delhi&quot;})</span></div><div class='arrow'>→</div><div class='step'><h4>⚙️ 3. Application</h4><p>Executes local code, gets live data, and returns it to LLM.</p></div></div></div>\"></iframe>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Structured Output Generation Review",
            "question": "Drag and drop the correct term into each blank.",
            "template": [
              "Function Calling allows LLMs to use external ____.",
              "The application executes the requested ____.",
              "XML organizes information using ____.",
              "A schema acts as a data ____."
            ],
            "options": [
              "tools",
              "blueprint",
              "tags",
              "function",
              "agents",
              "tokens",
              "datasets"
            ],
            "answers": {
              "blank_1": "tools",
              "blank_2": "function",
              "blank_3": "tags",
              "blank4": "blueprint"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Hands-On: Product Information Extractor",
            "difficulty": "Easy",
            "question": "You are building an online shopping application. Complete the prompt so the LLM extracts product information into the specified JSON schema.",
            "starterCode": "import json\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nproduct_text = \"Apple iPhone 15 Pro costs $999 and comes with 256GB storage.\"\n\ndef extract_product(text):\n    # TODO: Write the prompt below.\n    prompt = f\"\"\"    [Write your prompt here]   \"\"\"\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        response_format={\"type\": \"json_object\"}\n    )\n\n    return response.choices[0].message.content",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "{\n  \"product_name\": \"Apple iPhone 15 Pro\",\n  \"price\": 999,\n  \"storage\": \"256GB\"\n}",
            "hint": "Provide the exact JSON schema inside your prompt and instruct the model to return only valid JSON.",
            "solution": "import json\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nproduct_text = \"Apple iPhone 15 Pro costs $999 and comes with 256GB storage.\"\n\ndef extract_product(text):\n    # TODO: Write the prompt below.\n    prompt = \"\"\"    You are an information extraction assistant.\n\nExtract the product details from the text below.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object using this exact schema:\n{\n  'product_name': ' ',\n  'price': 0,\n  'storage': ' '\n}\n\nDo not return explanations or markdown.\n\nProduct Description:\n{text}    \"\"\"\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        response_format={\"type\": \"json_object\"}\n    )\n\n    return response.choices[0].message.content"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Hands-On: Receipt Information Extractor",
            "difficulty": "Easy",
            "question": "A coffee shop wants to digitize printed receipts. Complete the prompt so the LLM extracts the store name and total amount into the specified JSON schema.",
            "starterCode": "import json\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nreceipt_text = \"Star Coffee. Date: 2025-11-12. Items: Latte x2, Blueberry Muffin x1. Total: $18.50. Thank you for visiting!\"\n\ndef extract_receipt(text):\n    # TODO: Write the prompt below.\n    prompt = f\"\"\"    [Write your prompt here]    \"\"\"\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        response_format={\"type\": \"json_object\"}\n    )\n\n    return response.choices[0].message.content",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "{\n  \"store_name\": \"Star Coffee\",\n  \"total_amount\": \"$18.50\"\n}",
            "hint": "Provide the exact JSON schema inside your prompt and instruct the model to return only valid JSON.",
            "solution": "import json\nfrom openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nreceipt_text = \"Star Coffee. Date: 2025-11-12. Items: Latte x2, Blueberry Muffin x1. Total: $18.50. Thank you for visiting!\"\n\ndef extract_receipt(text):\n    # TODO: Write the prompt below.\n    prompt = \"\"\"You are an information extraction assistant.\n\nExtract the receipt details from the text below.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object using this exact schema:\n{{\n  \"store_name\": \"\",\n  \"total_amount\": \"\"\n}}\n\nDo not return explanations or markdown.\n\nReceipt:\n{text}\n\"\"\"\n\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n        response_format={\"type\": \"json_object\"}\n    )\n\n    return response.choices[0].message.content"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "scenario",
          "title": "The Broken Frontend API",
          "description": "You are building an AI API Response Generator that dynamically creates UI components based on user requests. The Next.js frontend expects the AI to return an array of objects to map over. However, about 10% of the time, the LLM wraps the JSON in backticks (```json ... ```), which causes the `JSON.parse()` function in your frontend to throw a fatal error. How do you permanently fix this architecture?",
          "choices": [
            {
              "text": "Add 'Please do not use backticks' to the end of the user prompt.",
              "outcome": "Incorrect. Polite requests do not mathematically constrain the model's token distribution effectively.",
              "score": 0
            },
            {
              "text": "Enable the 'JSON Mode' parameter in the API call and use a strict validation library (like Zod) on the backend to strip any rogue markdown before sending it to the frontend.",
              "outcome": "Correct! Enforcing native API JSON mode combined with a programmatic validation and cleaning layer ensures that your frontend never receives breaking string formats.",
              "score": 100
            },
            {
              "text": "Switch from JSON output to XML output.",
              "outcome": "Incorrect. Next.js and modern web frameworks consume JSON natively. Switching to XML would require building heavy, unnecessary XML parsers.",
              "score": 10
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "Why is Structured Output Generation important in software applications?",
