              "blank_2": "vector",
              "blank_3": "dimension",
              "blank_4": "closer"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Open-Source vs. Closed-Source Models",
            "explanation": "Now that we know what embeddings are, we need a model to generate them.There are two common approaches.\n**1. Closed-Source (The Rented API):**\nExamples: OpenAI (`text-embedding-3`), Cohere, Anthropic.\nPros: Zero infrastructure setup; state-of-the-art accuracy out of the box.\nCons: You pay per token processed. Data privacy risk (your data leaves your network).\n\n**2. Open-Source (The Owned Engine):**\nExamples: HuggingFace (`BGE-Large`, `all-MiniLM`).\nPros: 100% data privacy (runs completely local). Fixed cost (just server electricity). Highly customizable.\nCons: You must manage the GPU/CPU deployment infrastructure yourself.",
            "tip": "For heavily regulated industries (Healthcare/HIPAA, Finance, Defense), self-hosted Open-Source models are usually mandatory to prevent data leakage."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Practical Implementation of Embeddings",
            "explanation": "In real-world applications, developers rarely train embedding models from scratch. Instead, they use pre-trained embedding models to convert text into vectors. You can either use a Closed-Source API such as OpenAI or run an Open-Source model locally using Hugging Face. Both approaches generate embeddings, but the deployment, privacy, and cost considerations are different.",
            "html_code": "<div style='background:#0d1117;border-radius:12px;padding:18px;font-family:Consolas,monospace;color:#c9d1d9;overflow:auto;line-height:1.6;'><span style='color:#8b949e;'># Open-Source Embedding Model (Runs Locally)</span><br><span style='color:#79c0ff;'>from</span> sentence_transformers <span style='color:#79c0ff;'>import</span> SentenceTransformer<br><br>model = SentenceTransformer(<span style='color:#a5d6ff;'>\"all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"</span>)<br><br>text = <span style='color:#a5d6ff;'>\"I love Artificial Intelligence\"</span><br><br>embedding = model.encode(text)<br><br>print(embedding.shape)<br><br><span style='color:#8b949e;'># Output:</span><br><span style='color:#ffa657;'>(384,)</span><br><br><hr style='border:1px solid #374151;'><br><span style='color:#8b949e;'># Closed-Source Embedding Model (OpenAI API)</span><br><span style='color:#79c0ff;'>from</span> openai <span style='color:#79c0ff;'>import</span> OpenAI<br><br>client = OpenAI()<br><br>response = client.embeddings.create(<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;model=<span style='color:#a5d6ff;'>\"text-embedding-3-small\"</span>,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;input=<span style='color:#a5d6ff;'>\"I love Artificial Intelligence\"</span><br>)<br><br>embedding = response.data[0].embedding<br><br>print(len(embedding))<br><br><span style='color:#8b949e;'># Output:</span><br><span style='color:#ffa657;'>1536</span></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What is Vector Space?",
            "explanation": "After text is converted into embeddings, the vectors are placed inside a mathematical world called `Vector Space`. Think of it as a giant map where every word, sentence, or document has its own location.\n\n Similar concepts are placed close together, while unrelated concepts are placed far apart. For example, 'Cat' and 'Dog' appear near each other because both represent animals, while 'Cat' and 'Airplane' are much farther apart because they have very different meanings.\n\n During training, the model continuously adjusts these positions so that semantically similar concepts move closer together. This allows the AI to understand relationships, find similar documents, perform Semantic Search, and retrieve relevant information for RAG systems.\n\n **Simple Rule:**\n Smaller Distance = More Similar Meaning\n Larger Distance = Less Similar Meaning\n[IMAGE:/images/genai/vectordb/em3.png]\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Vector Space & Similarity Review",
            "introduction": "Excellent work! We now understand how embeddings are compared, how developers generate embeddings in real projects, and how vectors are organized inside a Vector Space. Let's do one final review before moving to Vector Databases.",
            "question": "Drag and drop the correct term into each blank.",
            "template": [
              "Cosine Similarity compares the ____ between vectors.",
