          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 2 & 3: Create Embeddings and Store Them",
            "explanation": "Now that the document has been divided into chunks, the next step is to create embeddings.Once you have your chunks, you pass them through an embedding model (like `text-embedding-3` or `BGE-large`). \n\nYou then store the resulting vectors in your Vector Database (Pinecone, ChromaDB, etc.). \n\n**Crucial Step:** You must store the *original text chunk* as Metadata alongside the vector. The vector is used for the math (searching), but when the database finds a match, it needs to return the human-readable text to the application.",
            "example": "Vector DB Record:\nID: \"chunk_001\"\nVector: [0.12, -0.45, ...]\nMetadata: {\"text\": \"Alex is an AI Engineer...\", \"source_doc\": \"resume.pdf\"}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 4, 5 & 6: User Query and Similarity Search",
            "explanation": "The knowledge base is now ready.Let's see what happens when a user asks a question.Suppose the user types:'Find React Developers'\n\n1. **User Query -> Embedding:** The system takes that exact text and passes it through the *same* embedding model used in Step 2. (Mixing different models will break the geometry completely).\n2. **Similarity Search:** The Vector DB compares the Query Vector against the millions of Chunk Vectors using Cosine Similarity (or Dot Product).\n3. **Return Relevant Chunks:** The database extracts the Top-K (e.g., Top 5) closest vectors, pulls the original text from their Metadata, and sends it back to your UI or your autonomous agent.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background: #1e293b; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #334155; font-family: monospace; color: #a78bfa;\"><div style=\"color: #fbbf24;\">User: \"Find React developers\"</div><div style=\"margin: 5px 0;\">⬇</div><div style=\"color: #34d399;\">Query Vector: [0.88, 0.11, ...]</div><div style=\"margin: 5px 0;\">⬇</div><div style=\"color: #60a5fa;\">Vector DB Search (Cosine Sim)</div><div style=\"margin: 5px 0;\">⬇</div><div style=\"color: #f472b6;\">Result: [\"chunk_82: Alex works with React and Python.\"]</div></div>"
          }
        },
