            "question": "A user asks 'Who won the Superbowl yesterday?'. Your vector DB returns documents with a confidence score of 0.3. Write a router function that returns 'WEB_SEARCH' if the score is below 0.7, and 'GENERATE' if it is above.",
            "starterCode": "def route_query(confidence_score):\n    # TODO: Implement the CRAG threshold routing\n    pass\n\nprint(route_query(0.3))",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "WEB_SEARCH",
            "hint": "Use a simple if/else statement checking if confidence_score < 0.7.",
            "solution": "def route_query(confidence_score):\n    if confidence_score < 0.7:\n        return \"WEB_SEARCH\"\n    else:\n        return \"GENERATE\"\n\nprint(route_query(0.3))"
          }
