        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Implementation - Step 1: Prepare the Document for Vectorless RAG",
            "explanation": "Now let's build a **Vectorless RAG** system from scratch using **PageIndex** and **Google Gemini**.\n\nIn this implementation, we will use a real **research paper (PDF)** instead of sample text. PageIndex will analyze the document, understand its structure, and build a hierarchical index. Later, we'll use this index to retrieve the most relevant sections without creating embeddings or using a Vector Database.\n\n### Implementation Workflow\n\nStep 1: Install the required libraries.\n\nStep 2: Import the required Python modules.\n\nStep 3: Initialize the PageIndex client.\n\nStep 4: Download the research paper from ArXiv.\n\nStep 5: Upload the PDF to PageIndex.\n\nIn the next slide, we'll wait for indexing to complete and then retrieve the relevant sections.\nResearch Paper We'll download the PDF directly from ArXiv.\n\n**PDF Link:**https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.12948.pdf\n\n### Install Required Libraries\n\n```bashpip install pageindex\npip install langchain\npip install langchain-google-genai\npip install google-generativeai\n```\n\n### Import Required Libraries\n\n```python import os\nimport json\nimport time\nimport asyncio\nimport requests\n\nfrom pageindex import PageIndexClient\nimport pageindex.utils as utils\n```\n\n### Initialize the PageIndex Client\n\n```pythonPAGEINDEX_API_KEY = \"YOUR_PAGEINDEX_API_KEY\"\n\npi_client = PageIndexClient(api_key=PAGEINDEX_API_KEY)\n```\n\n### Download the Research Paper\n\n```python\npdf_url = \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.12948.pdf\"\n\npdf_path = os.path.join(\"data\",pdf_url.split('/')[-1])\n\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(pdf_path),exist_ok=True)\n\nresponse = requests.get(pdf_url)\n\nwith open(pdf_path, \"wb\") as f:\n    f.write(response.content)\n\nprint(\"PDF Downloaded Successfully\")\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```text\nPDF Downloaded Successfully\n```\n\n### Submit the PDF to PageIndex\n\n```python\ndoc_info = pi_client.submit_document(pdf_path)\n\ndoc_id = doc_info[\"doc_id\"]\n\nprint(\"Document Submitted:\", doc_id)\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```text\nDocument Submitted: doc_8b2c91a7f34...\n```\n\nAt this point, the document has been uploaded successfully. However, PageIndex still needs to analyze the PDF and build its hierarchical document structure. In the next step, we'll wait for indexing to finish before performing Vectorless Retrieval."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Implementation - Step 2: Index the Document & Retrieve Relevant Sections",
            "explanation": "Now that the PDF has been uploaded to **PageIndex**, the system starts analyzing the document. During this process, it builds a **hierarchical document structure** by identifying chapters, headings, sections, and paragraphs.\n\nUnlike traditional RAG, no embeddings are created. Instead, PageIndex understands the document structure so the LLM can later reason about where the answer is located.\n\n### Implementation Workflow\n\nStep 6: Wait until indexing is complete.\n\nStep 7: Initialize the Gemini LLM.\n\nStep 8: Build the retrieval function.\n\nOnce indexing is finished, the document is ready for Vectorless Retrieval.\n\n### Wait for Indexing\n\n```python\nimport time\n\nprint(f\"Waiting for document {doc_id}...\")\n\nwhile not pi_client.is_retrieval_ready(doc_id):\n    print(\"Processing...\")\nif pi_client.is_retrieval_ready(doc_id):\n    print(\"Document Ready!\")\n    tree = pi_client.get_tree(\n    doc_id,node_summary=True)[\"result\"]\n    utils.print_tree(tree)\nelse:\n    tree=None\n```\n\nOutput\n\n```text\nWaiting for document...\nProcessing...\nProcessing...\nDocument Ready!\n\nChapter 1\n ├── Introduction\n ├── Methodology\n ├── Experiments\n └── Conclusion\n```\n\n### Initialize Gemini\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_google_genai import ChatGoogleGenerativeAI\nimport os\n\nos.environ[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"] = \"YOUR_GOOGLE_API_KEY\"\n\nllm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(\n    model=\"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    temperature=0.3\n)\n```\n\n### Build the Retrieval Function\n\n```python\ndef retrieve_from_pageindex(query, doc_id):\n\n    response = pi_client.submit_query(doc_id=doc_id, query=query)\n\n    retrieval_id = response[\"retrieval_id\"]\n\n    while True:\n\n        retrieval = pi_client.get_retrieval(retrieval_id)\n\n        if retrieval[\"status\"] == \"completed\":\n            break\n\n        time.sleep(1)\n\n    contexts = []\n\n    for node in retrieval[\"retrieved_nodes\"]:\n\n        for group in node[\"relevant_contents\"]:\n\n            for item in group:\n                contexts.append(item[\"relevant_content\"])\n\n    return contexts\n```\n\nThe retrieval function asks PageIndex to search the document. Instead of searching embeddings, PageIndex reasons over the document hierarchy and returns only the most relevant sections."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Implementation - Step 3: Build the Vectorless RAG Pipeline",
            "explanation": "The final step is to combine the **retrieved context** with the user's question and send both to the Large Language Model.\n\nThe LLM is instructed to answer **only using the retrieved context**. This reduces hallucinations and ensures the response comes directly from the document.\n\n### Build the Vectorless RAG Pipeline\n\n```python\ndef vectorless_rag(query, doc_id):\n\n    contexts = retrieve_from_pageindex(query, doc_id)\n\n    combined_context = \"\\n\\n\".join(contexts)\n\n    prompt = f\"\"\"\nYou are a research assistant.\nAnswer ONLY using the context.\nContext:{combined_context}\nQuestion:{query}\n\"\"\"\n\n    response = llm.invoke(prompt)\n\n    return response.content\n```\n\n### Ask a Question\n\n```python\nquery = \"What is the main contribution of this paper?\"\n\nanswer = vectorless_rag( query, doc_id)\n\nprint(answer)\n```\n\nExample Output\n\n```text\nThe paper's main contribution is showing that the reasoning abilities of large language models (LLMs) can be enhanced\nthrough pure reinforcement learning (RL), eliminating the need for human-annotated reasoning trajectories. It also explores the development of reasoning abilities in LLMs through self-evolution in a reinforcement learning (RL) framework with minimal human labeling. Additionally, the multi-stage pipeline of DeepSeek-R1 and the development of its models (DeepSeek-R1 Dev1, Dev2, and Dev3) constitute the main contribution of the paper.\n```\nCongratulations! 🎉 You have now built a complete **Vectorless RAG** pipeline. Unlike traditional RAG, this system does not generate embeddings or use a Vector Database. Instead, it relies on **PageIndex** to understand the document structure and uses the **Gemini LLM** to generate accurate answers from the retrieved sections."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "A research paper has already been uploaded and indexed using PageIndex. Complete the missing code to retrieve the relevant sections, combine the retrieved context, ask the LLM, and print the final answer.",
            "starterCode": "query = \"What is the main contribution of this paper?\"\n\n# Retrieve relevant sections\n\n\n# Combine the retrieved sections into one context\n\n\n# Create the prompt\nprompt = f\"\"\"\nContext:\n{combined_context}\n\nQuestion:\n{query}\n\"\"\"\n\n# Generate the answer\n\n\n# Print the answer\n",
            "solution": "query = \"What is the main contribution of this paper?\"\n\n# Retrieve relevant sections\ncontexts = retrieve_from_pageindex(query, doc_id)\n\n# Combine the retrieved sections into one context\ncombined_context = \"\\n\\n\".join(contexts)\n\n# Create the prompt\nprompt = f\"\"\"\nContext:\n{combined_context}\n\nQuestion:\n{query}\n\"\"\"\n\n# Generate the answer\nresponse = llm.invoke(prompt)\n\n# Print the answer\nprint(response.content)",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Use `retrieve_from_pageindex()` to retrieve the context, `join()` to combine it, `llm.invoke()` to generate the answer, and `response.content` to display it."
          }
        },
