    {
      "id": "M008-rag-07-evaluation",
      "title": "Evaluation & Observability (Production RAG)",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#0ea5e9",
        "accent": "#0369a1"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Vibecession: Moving from Vibes to Metrics",
            "explanation": "Welcome to the final stage of RAG mastery: Production. \n\nWhen you build a RAG app on your laptop, you test it by typing 3 questions. If the answers look good, you deploy it. This is called 'Vibe-based Evaluation'. It is the number one reason enterprise AI projects fail.\n\nYou cannot deploy a RAG system to thousands of users based on vibes. You must break the system into two halves and mathematically grade them:\n1. **Retrieval Evaluation:** Did the Vector DB find the right documents?\n2. **Generation Evaluation:** Did the LLM give a factual, relevant answer based on those documents?",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background: #0f172a; padding: 20px; border-radius: 12px; color: white; font-family: sans-serif; border: 1px solid #0ea5e9;\"><h4 style=\"color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 0; text-align: center;\">The RAG Evaluation Triad</h4><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; text-align: center;\"><div style=\"background: #1e293b; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border-top: 3px solid #8b5cf6;\"><b style=\"color: #a78bfa; font-size: 13px;\">Context Relevance</b><div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 5px;\">Did the DB pull garbage? (Query vs Context)</div></div><div style=\"background: #1e293b; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border-top: 3px solid #10b981;\"><b style=\"color: #34d399; font-size: 13px;\">Faithfulness</b><div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 5px;\">Did the LLM hallucinate? (Context vs Answer)</div></div><div style=\"background: #1e293b; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; border-top: 3px solid #f59e0b;\"><b style=\"color: #fbbf24; font-size: 13px;\">Answer Relevance</b><div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 5px;\">Did it actually answer the user? (Query vs Answer)</div></div></div></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Retrieval Metrics: Precision@K & Recall@K",
            "explanation": "Let's grade the Vector Database first using standard search engine math.\n\n**Precision@K:** Out of the Top-K documents we retrieved, how many were actually relevant? If we pull 5 documents, and 2 are useful, our Precision is 40%.\n`Formula: (Relevant Docs in Top K) / K`\n\n**Recall@K:** Out of ALL the relevant documents in the entire database, how many did we find? If there are 10 total relevant documents hidden in the database, and we only pulled 2 of them in our Top-5, our Recall is 20%. \n`Formula: (Relevant Docs in Top K) / (Total Relevant Docs in DB)`",
            "example": "Database contains 10 relevant documents.\n\nTop-5 Retrieved Documents:\n[D1, D2, D3, D4, D5] #D1 & D2 Correct and D3,D4 & D5 are not correct\n\nPrecision@5 = 2 / 5 = 0.40 = 40%\n(Only 2 of the 5 retrieved documents were relevant)\n\nRecall@5 = 2 / 10 = 0.20 = 20%\n(We found only 2 out of 10 relevant documents in the database)\n\n`Key Idea:` Precision measures retrieval quality, while Recall measures retrieval coverage.",
            "tip": "High Precision means no garbage. High Recall means nothing important was left behind."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Retrieval Metrics: MRR & NDCG",
            "explanation": "Precision and Recall don't care about **order**. But in RAG, order is everything! (The LLM pays the most attention to the first document).\n\n**MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank):** This metric only cares about the FIRST correct answer. If the first relevant document is at Rank #1, score = 1.0. If it's at Rank #4, score = 0.25.\n`Formula: 1 / (Rank of FIRST relevant document)`\n\n**NDCG (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain):** The holy grail of ranking metrics. It gives you a perfect 1.0 if every document is perfectly ranked from most relevant to least relevant. It heavily penalizes the system if a highly relevant document is buried at Rank #5, using logarithms.\n`Formula: DCG / Ideal_DCG (where DCG sums the relevance divided by log2 of the rank)`",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; font-family: monospace; color: #166534;\"><b style=\"font-size: 14px;\">NDCG Intuition Check:</b><br><br>Retrieval A: [Perfect Doc, Bad Doc, Okay Doc]<br>Retrieval B: [Bad Doc, Okay Doc, Perfect Doc]<br><br><span style=\"color: #047857;\">Both have the exact same Precision (2/3). But Retrieval A has a massively higher NDCG score because the Perfect Doc is at the top!</span></div>",
            "example": "MRR Example:\nRank 1 → Not relevent\nRank 2 →Not relevent \nRank 3 →  First Relevant Document\n\nMRR = 1 / 3 = 0.33\n\nNDCG Example:\nIdeal: [Perfect, Good, Fair]\nActual: [Fair, Good, Perfect]\n\nNDCG < 1 because the best document is not at the top.\n\n`Key Idea:` MRR cares about the first correct result. NDCG cares about the entire ranking order."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Calculate: Precision and MRR",
            "difficulty": "Easy",
            "question": "You retrieved K=4 documents. The relevance array is [0, 1, 0, 1] (0 is bad, 1 is relevant). Write the Python to calculate Precision@4 and MRR.",
            "starterCode": "retrieved = [0, 1, 0, 1]\nk = len(retrieved)\n\n# TODO: Calculate Precision\nprecision = \n\n# TODO: Calculate MRR (Remember python is 0-indexed, but Rank is 1-indexed!)\nmrr = \n\nprint(f\"Precision: {precision}, MRR: {mrr}\")",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "Precision: 0.5, MRR: 0.5",
            "hint": "Precision is sum(retrieved)/k. For MRR, the first '1' is at index 1, which is Rank 2. So MRR = 1/2.",
            "solution": "retrieved = [0, 1, 0, 1]\nk = len(retrieved)\n\n# Calculate Precision\nprecision = sum(retrieved) / k\n\n# Calculate MRR\nmrr = 0\nfor index, is_relevant in enumerate(retrieved):\n    if is_relevant == 1:\n        mrr = 1.0 / (index + 1) # Rank is index + 1\n        break\n\nprint(f\"Precision: {precision}, MRR: {mrr}\")"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Generation Metrics: LLM-as-a-Judge",
            "explanation": "We graded the Vector DB. Now we must grade the LLM's text output.\nHow do you write a Python script to check if an essay is 'faithful' to a source document? You can't. Python doesn't understand English nuance.\n\nSo, we use **LLM-as-a-Judge**.\nWe write a system prompt for a 'Judge LLM' (usually GPT-4) to read the Context and the drafted Answer, and assign a score from 1 to 5 for **Faithfulness** (no hallucinations).\n\nIf the RAG LLM says 'The sky is green', the Judge LLM reads the context document, sees 'The sky is blue', and outputs: `{\"score\": 0, \"reason\": \"Hallucination detected regarding sky color.\"}`",
            "example": "To prevent bias, the Judge LLM should be a different, larger model than the RAG LLM (e.g., Llama 3 8B generates the answer, GPT-4 evaluates it)."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Automated Frameworks: RAGAS & DeepEval",
            "explanation": "You don't need to write the LLM-as-a-Judge prompts yourself. The industry has standardized this into powerful Python testing frameworks.\n\n**RAGAS (RAG Assessment)**\nAutomatically evaluates RAG systems using metrics like Faithfulness, Answer Relevance, Context Precision, and Context Recall.\nIt helps measure whether retrieved documents actually support the generated answer.\n\n**DeepEval**\nThink of this as `pytest` for AI. It integrates directly into your CI/CD pipeline. Every time you push new code, DeepEval can automatically test your RAG system and fail deployment if quality scores drop below your threshold.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background:#1e1e1e;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #333;overflow:hidden;font-family:'Fira Code',Consolas,monospace;color:#d4d4d4;font-size:13px;box-shadow:0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\"><div style=\"background:#2d2d2d;padding:8px 15px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;border-bottom:1px solid #1e1e1e;\"><div style=\"width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:#ff5f56;\"></div><div style=\"width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:#ffbd2e;\"></div><div style=\"width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:#27c93f;\"></div><span style=\"margin-left:10px;color:#858585;font-size:12px;\">evaluate_rag.py</span></div><div style=\"padding:15px;line-height:1.6;\"><span style=\"color:#6a9955;\"># RAGAS Evaluation</span><br><span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">from</span> ragas <span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">import</span> evaluate<br><span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">from</span> ragas.metrics <span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">import</span> faithfulness, answer_relevancy<br><br>result = <span style=\"color:#dcdcaa;\">evaluate</span>(dataset, metrics=[faithfulness, answer_relevancy])<br><span style=\"color:#569cd6;\">print</span>(result)<br><br><span style=\"color:#6a9955;\"># DeepEval Testing</span><br><span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">from</span> deepeval <span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">import</span> assert_test<br><span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">from</span> deepeval.metrics <span style=\"color:#c586c0;\">import</span> FaithfulnessMetric<br><br>metric = <span style=\"color:#4ec9b0;\">FaithfulnessMetric</span>(threshold=<span style=\"color:#b5cea8;\">0.8</span>)<br><span style=\"color:#dcdcaa;\">assert_test</span>(test_case, [metric])</div></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Build a Mini RAG Evaluator",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "Count how many retrieved documents are relevant and calculate Precision@K automatically.",
            "starterCode": "retrieved = [1, 1, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1]\n\n# TODO: Count relevant documents\n# TODO: Calculate Precision\n\nprint(precision)",
            "expected_output": "0.5714285714285714",
            "hint": "Precision = sum(retrieved) / len(retrieved)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "scenario",
