            "starterCode": "from trl import DPOTrainer, DPOConfig\n\n# Configure DPO training\ndpo_config = DPOConfig(\n    output_dir=___,\n    num_train_epochs=___,\n    per_device_train_batch_size=___,\n    gradient_accumulation_steps=___,\n    learning_rate=___,\n    beta=___,\n    lr_scheduler_type=___\n)\n\n# Create trainer\ntrainer = DPOTrainer(\n    model=___,\n    ref_model=___,\n    args=___,\n    train_dataset=___,\n    tokenizer=___\n)",
            "solution": "from trl import DPOTrainer, DPOConfig\n\ndpo_config = DPOConfig(\n    output_dir='./dpo_results',\n    num_train_epochs=1,\n    per_device_train_batch_size=2,\n    gradient_accumulation_steps=8,\n    learning_rate=5e-7,\n    beta=0.1,\n    lr_scheduler_type='cosine'\n)\n\ntrainer = DPOTrainer(\n    model=model,\n    ref_model=None,\n    args=dpo_config,\n    train_dataset=dpo_dataset,\n    tokenizer=tokenizer\n)",
            "hint": "DPO uses much lower learning rate (5e-7) than SFT. Set ref_model=None for implicit reference. beta=0.1 is the standard.",
            "explanation": "DPOTrainer directly optimizes the model to prefer 'chosen' over 'rejected' responses. The low learning rate prevents destroying SFT knowledge. beta=0.1 provides moderate preference enforcement. ref_model=None uses the initial model state as the implicit reference.",
            "concepts": [
