        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Checkpointers: Persistent Agent Memory",
            "explanation": "Your LangGraph agent can now reason, use tools, and loop — but it forgets everything between invocations. It's the goldfish problem all over again! Just like we added Memory to LangChain chains earlier, we need persistence for our graph agents.\n\n**🧒 The Video Game Save Point Analogy:**\n\nImagine playing a video game without save points. Every time you turn off the console, you start from Level 1. That would be terrible, right?\n\nA Checkpointer IS the save point for your agent. After every node executes, the checkpointer automatically saves the agent's entire state — like an auto-save in a video game. You can resume from any checkpoint, replay steps, or even go back in time!\n\n**The Problem Without Checkpointers:**\n```python\nresult1 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'My name is Alice')]})\n# Agent: 'Nice to meet you, Alice!'\n\nresult2 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'What is my name?')]})\n# Agent: 'I don\\'t know your name.'  ← Forgot everything!\n```\n\n**MemorySaver (Your Dev Save Point):**\n```python\nfrom langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver\n\ncheckpointer = MemorySaver()\ngraph = graph_builder.compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n```\n\nStores state in RAM. Perfect for development — but data vanishes when the process restarts.\n\n**🔑 Thread IDs — Separate Save Files:**\nEach conversation needs a unique `thread_id` — like having separate save files for different game playthroughs:\n\n```python\nconfig = {'configurable': {'thread_id': 'conversation_001'}}\n\nresult = graph.invoke(\n    {'messages': [('human', 'My name is Alice')]},\n    config=config\n)\n\n# Same thread_id = same save file = agent remembers!\nresult2 = graph.invoke(\n    {'messages': [('human', 'What is my name?')]},\n    config=config\n)\n# Agent: 'Your name is Alice!'  ✅\n```\n\n**🏭 Production Checkpointers:**\n• `PostgresSaver` — PostgreSQL database (recommended for production)\n• `SqliteSaver` — SQLite file (good for small apps)\n• `RedisSaver` — Redis cache (blazing fast)\n\n**🔑 The Golden Rule:**\n`MemorySaver` for development. `PostgresSaver` for production. ALWAYS pass `thread_id` in config.\n\nLet's add memory to an agent."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "language": "python",
            "title": "Adding Memory with MemorySaver",
            "difficulty": "Easy",
            "question": "Add persistent memory to a compiled graph. Import MemorySaver from langgraph.checkpoint.memory, create a checkpointer instance, and compile the graph with it. Store the compiled graph in 'graph'.",
            "starterCode": "from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import ___\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph\nfrom typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\ndef chatbot(state):\n    return {'messages': ['Hello!']}\n\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\ngraph_builder.add_node('chatbot', chatbot)\ngraph_builder.set_entry_point('chatbot')\ngraph_builder.set_finish_point('chatbot')\n\n# Create checkpointer and compile\ncheckpointer = ___\ngraph = graph_builder.compile(___)",
            "solution": "from langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph\nfrom typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\ndef chatbot(state):\n    return {'messages': ['Hello!']}\n\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\ngraph_builder.add_node('chatbot', chatbot)\ngraph_builder.set_entry_point('chatbot')\ngraph_builder.set_finish_point('chatbot')\n\ncheckpointer = MemorySaver()\ngraph = graph_builder.compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)",
            "hint": "Import MemorySaver, create it with MemorySaver(), then pass checkpointer=checkpointer to compile().",
