        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Agent Failure Analysis & Debugging",
            "explanation": "Here's a mindset shift that will make you a much better agent engineer: **Understanding WHY agents fail is more valuable than understanding why they succeed.** Anyone can build a demo that works on the happy path. Production engineers build systems that fail gracefully and are easy to debug.\n\n**The Crash Investigation Analogy:**\n\nWhen an airplane crashes, investigators don't just note \"the plane crashed.\" They reconstruct the entire flight — every instrument reading, every radio call, every pilot decision — to find the exact moment things went wrong. They call it the \"chain of events.\"\n\nAgent debugging works exactly the same way. You need to reconstruct the agent's entire trajectory — every thought, action, observation, and decision — to find where it went off the rails.\n\n**The 6 Most Common Agent Failures — And How to Fix Each:**\n\n**1. 🎭 Hallucinated Tool Calls** — Agent invents tools that don't exist\n```\nAgent: I'll use the 'analyze_sentiment' tool...\nSystem: ERROR: No tool named 'analyze_sentiment'\n```\n**Root Cause:** Tool descriptions are unclear, or the agent doesn't have the right tool for the job\n**Fix:** Clear tool descriptions + strict tool whitelist + add the tools the agent actually needs\n\n**2. 🔄 Infinite Loops** — Same tool call repeated over and over\n```\nStep 5: search('AI agents')\nStep 6: search('AI agents')  ← Same call!\nStep 7: search('AI agents')  ← Stuck!\n```\n**Root Cause:** Agent doesn't recognize it's repeating itself\n**Fix:** Max iterations + duplicate detection (if last 3 actions are identical, force stop)\n\n**3. 🎯 Goal Drift** — Agent forgets the original task after 10+ steps\n```\nUser: \"Compare AAPL and MSFT stock performance\"\nStep 15: Agent is now researching cryptocurrency regulations...\n```\n**Root Cause:** Original goal gets buried as context window fills up\n**Fix:** Re-inject the original goal every N steps as a system message\n\n**4. ⏹️ Premature Termination** — Agent stops too early with incomplete results\n```\nUser: \"Research 5 competitors\"\nAgent: \"I found 2 competitors. Here they are.\" (stops)\n```\n**Root Cause:** Agent's completion criteria are too loose\n**Fix:** Clear completion criteria in the system prompt: \"You MUST find at least 5 competitors before stopping\"\n\n**5. 💥 Context Window Overflow** — Too many messages crash the model\n**Root Cause:** No context management strategy\n**Fix:** Summarization + sliding window (Phase 8 strategies)\n\n**6. 🏗️ Cascading Failures** — One agent fails → feeds bad data → next agent fails worse\n**Root Cause:** No validation at handoff points\n**Fix:** Validate outputs at every handoff (use Pydantic models)\n\n**Your Debugging Toolkit:**\n\n| Tool | What It Does | When to Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| **LangSmith** | Visualizes every step as a trace tree | Default choice for LangGraph agents |\n| **Arize Phoenix** | Open-source LLM tracing | When you want self-hosted observability |\n| **OpenTelemetry** | Industry-standard distributed tracing | Enterprise integrations |\n| **Custom Logging** | Log every (Thought, Action, Observation) | Always — this is your minimum |\n\n**The Golden Rule of Agent Debugging:**\nAlways log the complete trajectory. For every iteration, log:\n```python\nlog_entry = {\n    'step': step_number,\n    'thought': llm_reasoning,        # What the agent was thinking\n    'action': tool_name,             # What it decided to do\n    'arguments': tool_args,          # What arguments it passed\n    'observation': tool_result,      # What the tool returned\n    'tokens_used': token_count,      # How many tokens this step cost\n    'timestamp': datetime.now()      # When this happened\n}\n```\n\nWhen something goes wrong, replay the trajectory. You'll find the exact step where the agent's reasoning broke down — just like a crash investigator finds the exact moment of failure.\n\nWith safety and debugging mastered, let's move on to the final analytical skill: evaluating your agent's performance systematically."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "scenario",
