          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Redis: The Ultra-Fast In-Memory Database",
            "explanation": "Most databases store data on disk (hard drive). This is durable but relatively slow. **Redis stores everything in RAM** — the same memory your CPU uses to run programs. RAM is 100,000x faster to access than a disk.\n\nThis makes Redis insanely fast:\n- Read: **under 0.1 milliseconds** (vs 5-10ms for a disk database)\n- Writes: **1 million operations per second**\n\n**How AI Engineers Use Redis:**\n\n**1. Response Caching — Stop Paying for Duplicate LLM Calls:**\n```python\nimport redis\nimport hashlib\nimport json\n\nr = redis.Redis(host='localhost', port=6379)\n\ndef get_ai_response(prompt: str) -> str:\n    # Create a cache key from the prompt\n    cache_key = hashlib.md5(prompt.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n    # Check if we already have this answer\n    cached = r.get(cache_key)\n    if cached:\n        return json.loads(cached)  # Return instantly, zero API cost\n\n    # Call the expensive LLM API\n    response = call_openai(prompt)\n\n    # Cache for 1 hour (3600 seconds)\n    r.setex(cache_key, 3600, json.dumps(response))\n    return response\n```\n\nIf 1,000 users ask \"What is RAG?\" on the same day, you only call OpenAI ONCE. The other 999 users get the cached response instantly at zero cost.\n\n**2. Session State — Fast Chat History:**\n```python\n# Store user's chat history in Redis (auto-expires in 24 hours)\nsession_key = f'session:{user_id}:{session_id}'\nr.setex(session_key, 86400, json.dumps(messages))\n```\n\n**3. Rate Limiting — Prevent API Abuse:**\n```python\n# Allow max 10 requests per minute per user\nrate_key = f'rate:{user_id}'\ncurrent = r.incr(rate_key)  # Increment counter\nif current == 1:\n    r.expire(rate_key, 60)  # Expire after 60 seconds\nif current > 10:\n    raise Exception('Rate limit exceeded')\n```"
          }
        },
        {
