        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Guardrails — Keeping LLMs From Going Off the Rails",
            "explanation": "LLMs are powerful but unpredictable. Without guardrails, your AI can produce harmful content, leak private data, or ignore its instructions entirely.\n\n**What Are Guardrails?**\nGuardrails are validation layers that check LLM inputs AND outputs before they reach the user:\n\n```\nUser Input → [Input Guardrail] → LLM → [Output Guardrail] → User\n```\n\n**Input Guardrails (Before the LLM):**\n```python\ndef input_guardrail(user_message: str) -> str:\n    # 1. Check for prompt injection attempts\n    if detect_prompt_injection(user_message):\n        return \"I can't process that request.\"\n    \n    # 2. Check for PII (Personal Identifiable Information)\n    if contains_pii(user_message):\n        user_message = redact_pii(user_message)\n    \n    # 3. Check content is on-topic\n    if not is_on_topic(user_message, allowed_topics):\n        return \"I can only help with questions about our product.\"\n    \n    # 4. Check token length to prevent cost abuse\n    if count_tokens(user_message) > MAX_INPUT_TOKENS:\n        return \"Your message is too long. Please shorten it.\"\n    \n    return user_message  # Safe to send to LLM\n```\n\n**Output Guardrails (After the LLM):**\n```python\ndef output_guardrail(llm_response: str) -> str:\n    # 1. Check for hallucinated information\n    if not is_faithful_to_context(llm_response, retrieved_docs):\n        return \"I'm not confident in this answer. Let me try again.\"\n    \n    # 2. Check for toxic or harmful content\n    if is_toxic(llm_response):\n        return \"I apologize, but I can't provide that response.\"\n    \n    # 3. Check for data leakage (system prompt, API keys)\n    if leaks_system_prompt(llm_response):\n        return \"I can help you with product questions!\"\n    \n    # 4. Validate structured output format\n    if not is_valid_json(llm_response):\n        return retry_with_format_instructions()\n    \n    return llm_response  # Safe to show to user\n```\n\n**NeMo Guardrails by NVIDIA:**\nNVIDIA's open-source framework for building guardrails with a simple configuration language:\n\n```yaml\n# config.yml\nmodels:\n  - type: main\n    engine: openai\n    model: gpt-4o-mini\n\nrails:\n  input:\n    flows:\n      - check_jailbreak\n      - check_pii\n      - check_topic\n  output:\n    flows:\n      - check_hallucination\n      - check_toxicity\n      - check_facts\n```\n\n**Guardrails AI — Python-Native Validation:**\n```python\nfrom guardrails import Guard\nfrom guardrails.hub import ToxicLanguage, CompetitorCheck\n\nguard = Guard().use_many(\n    ToxicLanguage(on_fail='exception'),\n    CompetitorCheck(competitors=['CompetitorA', 'CompetitorB'])\n)\n\nresult = guard(\n    model='gpt-4o-mini',\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': user_message}]\n)\n# Automatically blocks toxic or competitor-mentioning responses!\n```\n\nGuardrails are not optional in production. They're the seatbelts of your AI application."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "scenario",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Customer Support Bot Gone Wrong",
            "description": "You deployed an AI customer support bot for an e-commerce company. Within the first week, the following incidents occur:\n\n1. A user tricks the bot into revealing the system prompt\n2. The bot recommends a competitor's product when asked for alternatives\n3. The bot provides incorrect refund policy information (hallucination)\n4. A user sends their credit card number in the chat\n\nWhich guardrail strategy addresses ALL of these issues?",
            "choices": [
              {
                "text": "Add a disclaimer saying 'AI responses may be inaccurate' and hope users read it",
                "score": 0,
                "outcome": "Disclaimers don't prevent the problems — they just shift liability. Users will still get wrong information, and the company's reputation suffers."
              },
              {
                "text": "Implement input guardrails (PII detection, prompt injection detection) AND output guardrails (faithfulness check, competitor filter, system prompt leak detection)",
                "score": 100,
