          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Observability — Seeing Inside Your AI Pipeline",
            "explanation": "When your AI gives a bad response, can you explain WHY? Observability gives you X-ray vision into every step of your AI pipeline.\n\n**The Observability Problem:**\nA user reports: 'Your AI gave me wrong information about my account.'\n\nWithout observability, you have NO idea:\n- What the user actually asked\n- What context the RAG system retrieved\n- What prompt was sent to the LLM\n- What the LLM's raw response was\n- How long each step took\n- How much it cost\n\n**LLM Tracing — The Core of Observability:**\nTracing records every step of your AI pipeline with timestamps, inputs, and outputs:\n\n```python\n# LangSmith tracing (automatic with LangChain)\nimport os\nos.environ['LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2'] = 'true'\nos.environ['LANGCHAIN_API_KEY'] = 'your-key'\n\n# Every LangChain call is now automatically traced!\n# You can see in the LangSmith dashboard:\n# - User input\n# - Retrieved documents (RAG)\n# - Full prompt sent to LLM\n# - LLM response\n# - Token count and cost\n# - Latency per step\n```\n\n**What to Log (The Essential Telemetry):**\n\n```python\nimport logging\nimport time\n\nasync def traced_chat(query: str):\n    trace = {\n        'trace_id': generate_id(),\n        'timestamp': datetime.utcnow(),\n        'user_query': query,\n    }\n    \n    # 1. RAG Retrieval\n    start = time.time()\n    docs = vector_db.search(query, k=5)\n    trace['retrieval_time_ms'] = (time.time() - start) * 1000\n    trace['retrieved_docs'] = [d.id for d in docs]\n    \n    # 2. LLM Call\n    start = time.time()\n    response = await llm.chat(build_prompt(query, docs))\n    trace['llm_time_ms'] = (time.time() - start) * 1000\n    trace['model'] = 'gpt-4o-mini'\n    trace['input_tokens'] = response.usage.prompt_tokens\n    trace['output_tokens'] = response.usage.completion_tokens\n    trace['cost_usd'] = calculate_cost(response.usage)\n    trace['response'] = response.content\n    \n    # 3. Save trace\n    save_trace(trace)\n    \n    return response.content\n```\n\n**Key Observability Platforms:**\n- **LangSmith** — Built for LangChain, best tracing UX, prompt playground\n- **Langfuse** — Open-source alternative to LangSmith, self-hostable\n- **Weights & Biases** — Best for fine-tuning experiments and model comparison\n- **Phoenix (Arize)** — Great for embedding drift and retrieval analysis\n\n**The 3 Key Dashboards:**\n1. **Latency Dashboard**: P50, P95, P99 response times\n2. **Quality Dashboard**: Evaluation scores over time, hallucination rate\n3. **Cost Dashboard**: Daily/weekly API spend, cost per query, cost per user"
          }
