          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Prompt Management — Treating Prompts Like Code",
            "explanation": "In production, your prompt IS your product. Changing a single word can dramatically affect output quality, cost, and safety. Prompts deserve the same rigor as code.\n\n**The Prompt Management Problem:**\n- Developer A changes the system prompt on Tuesday\n- Quality drops 20% but nobody notices until Friday\n- Nobody remembers what the prompt said before Tuesday\n- There's no way to roll back\n\n**Prompt Versioning:**\nEvery prompt change should be versioned, tracked, and tested:\n\n```python\n# prompt_registry.py\nPROMPTS = {\n    'chat_v1': {\n        'version': '1.0.0',\n        'template': 'You are a helpful assistant. Answer concisely.',\n        'model': 'gpt-4o-mini',\n        'temperature': 0.7,\n        'created_at': '2025-01-15',\n        'eval_score': 0.82,\n    },\n    'chat_v2': {\n        'version': '2.0.0',\n        'template': 'You are a helpful assistant for {company}. '\n                    'Answer using only the provided context. '\n                    'If unsure, say \"I don\\'t know.\"',\n        'model': 'gpt-4o-mini',\n        'temperature': 0.3,\n        'created_at': '2025-02-01',\n        'eval_score': 0.91,\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**A/B Testing Prompts in Production:**\n```python\nimport random\n\ndef get_prompt(user_id: str) -> dict:\n    # Route 10% of traffic to new prompt\n    if hash(user_id) % 100 < 10:\n        return PROMPTS['chat_v2']  # Canary\n    return PROMPTS['chat_v1']      # Stable\n\n# Track metrics per version\n# If v2 scores higher → gradually increase to 100%\n# If v2 scores lower → roll back to v1\n```\n\n**Deployment Strategies:**\n- **Canary Deploy**: Route 5-10% of traffic to new prompt, monitor metrics, gradually increase\n- **Blue-Green**: Run both versions simultaneously, switch traffic instantly\n- **Shadow Mode**: Run new prompt in parallel but don't show results to users, compare offline\n\n**The Golden Rule:**\nNever change a production prompt without:\n1. Running your evaluation suite on the new version\n2. Comparing scores to the current production baseline\n3. Deploying via canary (not all-at-once)\n4. Monitoring metrics for at least 24 hours"
          }
        },
