            "explanation": "**Your Capstone Mission:**\n\nBuild a complete machine learning pipeline that takes raw data, trains a model, evaluates it, and deploys it to a cloud endpoint — with monitoring and automated retraining.\n\n**What You Will Build:**\nA \"Customer Churn Prediction System\" that predicts which customers are likely to cancel their subscription, deployed as a real-time prediction API on the cloud.\n\n**Project Requirements:**\n\n1. **Data Pipeline**:\n   - Ingest customer data (usage patterns, support tickets, billing)\n   - Feature engineering (recency, frequency, monetary value)\n   - Data validation and quality checks\n   - Train/test/validation split with stratification\n\n2. **Model Training**:\n   - Train multiple models (logistic regression, random forest, XGBoost)\n   - Hyperparameter tuning with cross-validation\n   - Track experiments with MLflow or Weights & Biases\n   - Model comparison and selection\n\n3. **Model Evaluation**:\n   - Precision, recall, F1, AUC-ROC curves\n   - Feature importance analysis\n   - Bias and fairness checks\n   - Calibration plots\n\n4. **Cloud Deployment**:\n   - Package model as a Docker container\n   - Deploy to cloud (AWS SageMaker, GCP Vertex AI, or Azure ML)\n   - Set up prediction API endpoint\n   - Implement batch prediction for bulk scoring\n\n5. **Monitoring & Retraining**:\n   - Monitor for data drift and model drift\n   - Set up alerts for performance degradation\n   - Automated retraining pipeline trigger\n   - A/B testing between model versions\n\n**Pipeline Architecture:**\n```\nRaw Data → Preprocessing → Feature Engineering → Model Training\n    → Evaluation → Registry → Deployment → Monitoring → Retrain\n```\n\n**Stretch Goals:**\n- Add explainability (SHAP values) to predictions\n- Build a dashboard for business users\n- Implement shadow deployment (new model runs alongside old)\n\nThis is real-world MLOps from start to finish!"
