          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "API Gateways: The Bouncer of Your System",
            "explanation": "An API Gateway is the single entry point for ALL traffic into your system. Think of it as a nightclub bouncer — it checks everyone's ID, controls how many people enter, and directs them to the right area.\n\n**Without an API Gateway:**\n- Any random person can flood your API with requests and your LLM bill skyrockets\n- No authentication means anyone can access your system\n- No logging means you have no idea who's doing what\n- Each service handles its own security leading to inconsistent protection\n\n**With an API Gateway:**\n- One place to enforce ALL security rules\n- Rate limiting prevents abuse\n- Authentication validates every request\n- Centralized logging captures everything\n- Request routing directs traffic to the right service\n\n**The 5 Core Responsibilities:**\n\n1. **Authentication** — Validates JWT tokens or API keys. Rejects unauthorized requests before they reach your backend.\n\n2. **Rate Limiting** — Controls how many requests each user can make. 10 requests/minute for free users, 100/minute for paid users.\n\n3. **Request Routing** — Directs traffic to the right service. Chat requests go to the chat service, search to the search service.\n\n4. **SSL/TLS Termination** — Handles HTTPS encryption. Internal services communicate over plain HTTP (faster).\n\n5. **Request/Response Logging** — Records every API call for debugging, analytics, and compliance.",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "sevenPoint",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "Popular API Gateway Options",
                    "body": "Kong (open-source, plugin-based), AWS API Gateway (fully managed, pay-per-request), Nginx (lightweight, manual config), Traefik (Kubernetes-native). For most AI startups, start with Nginx reverse proxy and upgrade to Kong when you need plugins."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "Rate Limiting Strategies",
                    "body": "Fixed Window: count requests per minute, reset at boundary. Sliding Window: count in a rolling 60-second window. Token Bucket: allow bursts up to a limit, then throttle. Best for LLM traffic patterns."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "API Versioning",
                    "body": "Always version your API: /api/v1/chat, /api/v2/chat. When you make breaking changes, deploy v2 alongside v1. Old clients keep working on v1 while new clients use v2."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "visual",
          "content": {
            "title": "API Gateway Request Flow",
            "description": "Every request passes through multiple security and routing checks before reaching your AI backend.",
            "type": "flow",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "client",
                "label": "Client Request",
                "description": "User sends a chat message from the frontend application"
              },
              {
                "id": "ssl",
                "label": "SSL/TLS Termination",
                "description": "HTTPS encryption is handled here. Internal traffic uses plain HTTP for speed"
