          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Scaling: From 10 to 1,000,000 Users",
            "explanation": "The architecture for 10 users will collapse at 1,000. Scaling requires evolving your architecture at each growth stage.\n\n**The Scaling Stages:**\n\n**10 Users:** Single FastAPI, SQLite, direct OpenAI calls. ~$50/month.\n\n**100 Users:** Switch to PostgreSQL + pgvector. Add Nginx + SSL. Rate limiting. ~$200/month.\n\n**1,000 Users:** Add Redis cache, Celery workers, model routing, LangSmith, Docker Compose. ~$1K/month.\n\n**10,000 Users:** Split into microservices. Kubernetes. Dedicated vector DB. AI gateway. ~$10K/month.\n\n**100,000 Users:** Multi-region. Self-hosted inference. RBAC. SOC 2 compliance. ~$100K+/month.\n\n**1,000,000 Users:** Global edge deployment. Custom hardware. ML-based routing. ~$500K+/month.\n\n**Golden Rules:**\n1. Scale horizontally before vertically\n2. Cache aggressively\n3. Measure before optimizing\n4. Plan for 10x, build for 3x\n5. Build incrementally"
          }
        },
