          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "AI Gateways: Your LLM Traffic Controller",
            "explanation": "An AI Gateway is a reverse proxy for LLM traffic. It sits between your app and LLM providers, providing unified API, failover, caching, cost tracking, and PII scrubbing.\n\n**Popular Options:**\n\n**LiteLLM (Open Source)** — Translates OpenAI-format requests to 100+ providers. Deploy as a Docker container.\n\n**OpenRouter (Managed)** — Single endpoint, routes to cheapest/best provider. One API key for all providers.\n\n**Custom Gateway** — Build with FastAPI for full control over PII scrubbing, cost tracking, compliance logging.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n1. Provider Abstraction — Change providers in config, not code\n2. Automatic Failover — OpenAI down? Route to Anthropic\n3. Cost Tracking — Know exact cost per request\n4. PII Scrubbing — Remove sensitive data before external APIs\n5. Centralized Logging — One place for all AI activity\n6. Caching — Avoid redundant calls across all services"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "visual",
          "content": {
            "title": "AI Gateway Architecture",
            "description": "The AI Gateway acts as a central control point between your application services and external LLM providers.",
