        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Enterprise GenAI Platform",
            "explanation": "Now let's bring everything together into one cohesive enterprise platform.\n\n**Core Components:**\n\n1. **Multi-Tenant Architecture** — Isolated vector stores, conversation histories, custom system prompts, per-tenant billing, row-level security.\n\n2. **Agent Layer** — Chat Agent (Q&A + RAG), Research Agent (web research), Data Agent (SQL generation), Code Agent (code execution). Each is a LangGraph subgraph.\n\n3. **MCP Integration** — Connect to Confluence, Salesforce, JIRA, Slack via MCP servers.\n\n4. **Deployment Pipeline:** GitHub -> CI (eval suite) -> Docker build -> Kubernetes staging -> Integration tests -> Production -> Monitor. Auto-rollback if error rate > 5%.\n\n5. **Success Metrics:**\n   - User satisfaction > 85%\n   - Agent success > 90%\n   - P95 TTFT < 1 second\n   - Cost per conversation < $0.10\n   - Zero PII leakage",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "sevenPoint",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "Start Small, Grow Big",
                    "body": "Don't build all of this on day one. Start with a single-tenant chat agent, add RAG, add monitoring, add security, add multi-tenancy. Each step delivers value."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "The Incremental Path",
                    "body": "Week 1: FastAPI + OpenAI. Week 2: PostgreSQL + pgvector RAG. Week 3: LangSmith. Week 4: Auth + rate limiting. Month 2: LangGraph agents. Month 3: MCP. Month 4+: Multi-tenancy and scaling."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "Key Architecture Decisions",
                    "body": "Which LLM providers? Managed vs self-hosted vector DB? Monolith vs microservices? Cloud provider? Open source vs managed? Make these early and document reasoning."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "code-example",
                "type": "code",
                "content": "```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Enterprise GenAI Platform\")\n\nclass GenAIPlatform:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.client = OpenAI()\n        self.cost_tracker = CostTracker()\n        self.pii_redactor = PIIRedactor()\n        self.circuit_breaker = CircuitBreaker()\n    \n    async def process(self, query, user_id, tenant_id):\n        # 1. Security: Redact PII\n        clean_query = self.pii_redactor.redact(query)\n        # 2. Cost: Route to optimal model\n        model = self.model_router.route(clean_query)\n        # 3. Performance: Check cache\n        cached = await self.cache.get(clean_query)\n        if cached: return cached\n        # 4. RAG: Retrieve with tenant isolation\n        context = await self.retrieve(clean_query, tenant_id)\n        # 5. Reliability: Call with circuit breaker\n        response = self.circuit_breaker.call(\n            self.client.chat.completions.create,\n            model=model,\n            messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": clean_query}]\n        )\n        # 6. Observability: Track cost\n        self.cost_tracker.track(model, input_tokens, output_tokens)\n        return response\n```"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
